                <pb facs="0668" n="568" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg568"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">251.11 Insull, Samuel/345: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacVeagh</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-03T14:00:00-05:00">March 3, 1934—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13. Please confirm Press Reports that the Minister for Foreign Affairs has
                    ordered Insull to leave Greece. Unless a definite date has been set for
                    expulsion you should make inquiry of the Foreign Minister <pb facs="0669"
                        n="569" xml:id="pg569"/> as to when he intends to give effect to the
                    assurances given to you especially that of February 16, and state that you are
                    doing so under instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
